/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:* repeatedly.  On the first invokation, and only the first invokation, the
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* flag member of the tabprm struct must be set to -1 to initialize memory
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* management, regardless of whether tabini() will actually be used to allocate
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* memory.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* Given:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   alloc     int       If true, allocate memory unconditionally for arrays in
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       the tabprm struct.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       If false, it is assumed that pointers to these arrays
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       have been set by the user except if they are null
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*                       first time (memory leaks may result if it had already
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       been initialized).
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* Function return value:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*             int       Status return value:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                         0: Success.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                         1: Null tabprm pointer passed.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                         2: Memory allocation failed.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                         3: Invalid tabular parameters.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       For returns > 1, a detailed error message is set in
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*                       values in the structs must be equal to the first 6
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       decimal places.  A value of 0 implies exact equality.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   tab1      const struct tabprm*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*                       The first tabprm struct to compare.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   tab2      const struct tabprm*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       The second tabprm struct to compare.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* Returned:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   equal     int*      Non-zero when the given structs are equal.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-* Function return value:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*             int       Status return value:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                         0: Success.
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*   sizes     int[2]    The first element is the base size of the struct as
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       returned by sizeof(struct tabprm).  The second element
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       is the total allocated size, in bytes, assuming that
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       the allocation was done by tabini().  This figure
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       includes memory allocated for the constituent struct,
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       tabprm::err.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       It is not an error for the struct not to have been set
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       up via tabset(), which normally results in additional
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*                       memory allocation. 
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     first time for a particular tabprm struct in order to initialize memory
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     management.  It must ONLY be used on the first initialization otherwise
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     memory leaks may result.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   int M
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     (Given or returned) Number of tabular coordinate axes.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     If tabini() is used to initialize the tabprm struct (as would normally
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     be the case) then it will set M from the value passed to it as a
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     function argument.  The user should not subsequently modify it.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   int *K
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     (Given or returned) Pointer to the first element of a vector of length
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     tabprm::M whose elements (K_1, K_2,... K_M) record the lengths of the
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     axes of the coordinate array and of each indexing vector.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     If tabini() is used to initialize the tabprm struct (as would normally
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     be the case) then it will set K from the array passed to it as a
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     function argument.  The user should not subsequently modify it.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   int *map
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     (Given) Pointer to the first element of a vector of length tabprm::M
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     that defines the association between axis m in the M-dimensional
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     coordinate array (1 <= m <= M) and the indices of the intermediate world
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     coordinate and world coordinate arrays, x[] and world[], in the argument
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     lists for tabx2s() and tabs2x().
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     When x[] and world[] contain the full complement of coordinate elements
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     in image-order, as will usually be the case, then map[m-1] == i-1 for
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     axis i in the N-dimensional image (1 <= i <= N).  In terms of the FITS
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     keywords
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     (Given) Pointer to the first element of a vector of length tabprm::M
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     whose elements contain the index value for the reference pixel for each
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     of the tabular coordinate axes.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*   double **index
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     (Given) Pointer to the first element of a vector of length tabprm::M of
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     pointers to vectors of lengths (K_1, K_2,... K_M) of 0-relative indexes
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     (see tabprm::K).
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     The address of any or all of these index vectors may be set to zero,
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     i.e.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-=       index[m] == 0;
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     this is interpreted as default indexing, i.e.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h:*     (Given) Pointer to the first element of the tabular coordinate array,
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     treated as though it were defined as
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-=       double coord[K_M]...[K_2][K_1][M];
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/tab.h-*     (see tabprm::K) i.e. with the M dimension varying fastest so that the
