/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* wcsnpv() - Memory allocation for PVi_ma
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* ---------------------------------------
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* wcsnpv() sets or gets the value of NPVMAX (default 64).  This global
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* variable controls the number of pvcard structs, for holding PVi_ma
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* keyvalues, that wcsini() should allocate space for.  It is also used by
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* wcsinit() as the default value of npvmax.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h:* possibly repeatedly.  On the first invokation, and only the first
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* invokation, wcsprm::flag must be set to -1 to initialize memory management,
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* regardless of whether wcsinit() will actually be used to allocate memory.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* Given:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*   alloc     int       If true, allocate memory unconditionally for the
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       crpix, etc. arrays.  Please note that memory is never
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       allocated by wcsinit() for the auxprm, tabprm, nor
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       wtbarr structs.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       If false, it is assumed that pointers to these arrays
--
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h:*                       initialized for the first time (memory leaks may
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       result if it had already been initialized).
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-* Given:
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*   npvmax    int       The number of PVi_ma keywords to allocate space for.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       If set to -1, the value of the global variable NPVMAX
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       will be used.  This is potentially thread-unsafe if
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       wcsnpv() is being used dynamically to alter its value.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*   npsmax    int       The number of PSi_ma keywords to allocate space for.
/testbed/cextern/wcslib/C/wcs.h-*                       If set to -1, the value of the global variable NPSMAX
--
